<title>UK: INSTANT VIEW - Outlook for UK interest rates.</title>
<headline>INSTANT VIEW - Outlook for UK interest rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a selection of comments on the outlook for UK interest rates based on Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown's budget statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>GLENN DAVIES, CHEIF ECONOMIST AT CREDIT LYONNAIS:</p>
<p>&quot;Although it (the net fiscal tightening in the budget) sounds pretty tight the consumer spending forecast of four percent for next year will worry the market a little bit, That's suggesting the consumer boom will continue. So I think that will suggest further base rate increases.</p>
</text>
